WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.161
Pimp My Ride fans may have believed the MTV
show acted like a fairy godmother for car

00:00:07.161 --> 00:00:09.510
lovers who couldn't afford tricked-out rides.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.340
Peek under the hood of this gearhead favorite,
however, and instead of finding a shiny V-8,

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.010
there might be a hamster on a wheel.

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:19.930
There's no arguing Pimp My Ride's popularity
and impact on pop culture, but the show's

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:23.670
behind-the-scenes reality makes the show seem
more like a lemon.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:26.490
Many cars with mechanical issues left with
the same problems

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.740
There's nothing glamorous about fixing a major
mechanical issue, and Pimp My Ride apparently

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.270
didn't try too hard.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.700
Instead, the crews seemed to use the cars
as elaborate advertisements for their sponsored

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.829
businesses by installing eye-catching fixtures.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:42.800
Some problems were fixed, but contestants
have claimed the labor was sloppy, while others

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.359
report the cars stopped working entirely days
later.

00:00:46.359 --> 00:00:50.949
One contestant, Seth Martino, said in his
Reddit AMA that his pimped car was a "polished

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:55.530
turd" that he couldn't even drive—until
he spent $1,700 of his own money to replace

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.870
the engine that the crews neglected to work
on.

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:58.870
But hey!

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:01.630
At least he got a robot arm that can ding
a triangle for some reason!

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:02.590
"Check that out."

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.500
"That thing is crazy!"

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.780
Great job, guys.

00:01:09.979 --> 00:01:12.180
The process took months

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:15.890
The show gives the impression that people
got their cars back days later, the paint

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:20.240
still wet, but some car owners report it actually
took upwards of seven months.

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.380
Shops had to order parts or make custom details
that required time.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:28.200
To top it off, former contestants told Huffington
Post that MTV didn't always provide an alternate

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:30.080
car for the entire time.

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:34.109
Seth Martino told HuffPo that they only paid
for a rental for the first two months—and

00:01:34.109 --> 00:01:38.829
worse, because of his young age, most reputable
companies wouldn't even rent a car to him.

00:01:38.829 --> 00:01:40.549
Bogus Backstories

00:01:40.549 --> 00:01:44.810
When contestants didn't seem interesting enough,
the show added some spice.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:47.900
Some cars were doctored to look worse in the
"before" shots.

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:51.560
Martino revealed in his AMA that producers
planted candy throughout his car.

00:01:51.560 --> 00:01:52.560
He wrote:

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:55.939
"I know I'm fat, but they went the extra mile
to make me look extra fat by telling the world

00:01:55.939 --> 00:01:59.259
that I kept candy all over my seat and floor
just in case I got hungry."

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:03.960
This begs the question: why humiliate a contestant
on a show with a guy who looks like this as

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:04.960
a regular cast-member?

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.940
Well, apparently the producers wanted a reason
to install a cotton candy machine.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.760
Worse, the cotton candy machine didn't have
a protective hood.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.580
Martino never even used it after the shoot.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.580
Surprised?

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.360
The element of surprise is great for good
television, and Pimp My Ride always started

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.090
with an unexpected knock on a jalopy-owner's
door.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:25.050
But how many do you really think answered
at just the right moment?

00:02:25.050 --> 00:02:27.390
That's why car owners were prepped beforehand.

00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:30.760
Some contestants knew they were finalists,
while others were already mic'ed up and ready

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.480
for retakes.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.950
Contestant Jake Glazier explained that producers
didn't think he seemed excited enough, so

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:37.550
they made him do it again.

00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.590
This is what faked overreaction looks like.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:44.010
Other times, if a person's house didn't seem
right for television, they'd go to a different

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.440
home altogether.

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:49.880
For a show starring a guy named Xzibit, they
sure did keep a bunch of weird stuff under

00:02:49.880 --> 00:02:50.880
wraps, huh?

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:51.880
"Alright you need two things.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.060
You need these, you've officially been pimped,
alright?

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:55.950
Get outa here..."

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:56.840
Thanks for watching!

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.700
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:02.692
And leave us a comment to let us know what
you thought was the sketchiest part of Pimp

00:03:02.692 --> 00:03:03.230
My Ride...

